config HANGAR_FS
	bool "Hangar: hangarfs, the environment's root"
	depends on FILE_LOCKING
	select FS_STACK
	select HANGAR_SYNC
	help
	  A thin stacking filesystem over a directory, passing every operation
	  through to it, which Hangar's guest agent mounts as an environment's
	  root over its overlayfs. Its own lock operations take a lock on a
	  file under a shared path for the environment as a whole (below)
	  before the local one.

config HANGAR_SYNC
	bool
	depends on FILE_LOCKING
	help
	  Locks taken on hangarfs files under paths Hangar's guest agent
	  registers are taken for the environment from the agent, through
	  /dev/hangar-sync, and given back when no process here holds one.
	  Without the agent, locks are local only.
